    ## The one thing a future worker must not repeat
    
    The dedicated platform is **part of the Sol action key**. Building any
    `//test/localization_sol:sol_tasks__*` target through `--config=remote` (or any
    other platform flag set) is a *different* action key: Bazel re-executes the real
    turns on a platform with **no `ACCESS_TOKEN` injection**, every one fails in
    ~250 ms, and the retained receipts are overwritten with those failures. This
    happened once (2026-10-08, all 88 overwritten).
    
    Recovery is cheap and was verified: re-running the documented `sol_arm` command
    restored **all 88** outputs from the Bazel action and remote cache — 219
    processes, 18 action-cache hits, 130 remote-cache hits, **0 executed Sol
    actions**. So a mis-keyed build costs no plan usage, but do not rely on it.
    
    Always use exactly:
    
    - `sol_route_check` (no provider call; reports token presence and JWT expiry)
    - `sol_first_task`
    - `sol_arm`
    
    from `services.yaml`. Never `--config=remote`.
    
